.TH "PB-CONFIG-LOCAL-ACCESS-PROXY-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-local-access-proxy-set - Set the machine reverse-proxy port


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config local-access proxy set <machine-alias> [port] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the port used by otherwise-unmapped app names on this machine. Port 80 is the automatic default. The selected port must already be authorized; numeric URLs and explicit aliases retain their destinations.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-local-access-proxy(1)\fP
